  "answer": "No. The stop did not fail. Someone started the lab again.\n\nAccount 645190837226 is sandbox5590 (owner hmoreau), assigned to GUID q7fwd. Its Babylon lifecycle actions, on cluster apac-1 (subject rhdp-apac.ocp-ai-serving.prod.q7fwd):\n\n| action | finished (UTC) | state |\n|---|---|---|\n| provision | 2026-09-24 03:02:41 | successful |\n| stop | 2026-09-28 18:06:12 | successful |\n| start | 2026-10-01 07:51:03 | successful |\n\nThe stop on 2026-09-28 completed successfully, and the cost data agrees with it. EC2 compute fell to 0.00 on 2026-09-29 and 2026-09-30. Then a start action ran on 2026-10-01 at 07:51 UTC, and compute resumed that day: 268.75 USD on 2026-10-01, then 331.20 USD a day on 10-02, 10-03 and 10-04. The lab has not been stopped again since.\n\nFor 2026-09-28 to 2026-10-05, EC2 compute (\"Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud - Compute\") was 1,473.75 USD. Of that, 211.40 USD is 2026-09-28 before the stop and 1,262.35 USD comes after the restart. EC2 - Other (EBS storage) adds 130.20 USD, which bills even while the lab is stopped, for a total of 1,603.95 USD.\n\nThe Babylon action records do not say who requested the start. Ask hmoreau whether it was started on purpose, and stop it again if it is not needed.\n"
